-- title:
--   Nodes of the resolved model index supersingular j-invariants
-- statement:
--   Let $p \ge 5$ be a prime, let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p` (the package of data and properties attached to the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of $X_0(p)$ built from the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,p$ and the coordinate $j = \mathrm{IgusaScheme.jFull}\,p$), let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to k$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a `DRResolvedModelPackage p 𝔛 O k toκ`. The assertion is that there is a bijection $a$ from the node index type $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{node}$ onto $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,k$, the set of those $j \in k$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $j$ has no nonzero $p$-torsion point, with the following property for each node $n$. Transport $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{nodeEquiv}\,n$, a point of the fibre product of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$, by the first projection followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, obtaining a point $x_n$ of the base change $\mathcal X_O$ of `DRModel p` along $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb Z$. Then $x_n$ lies in the preimage under the first projection of the open image of the finite-$j$ chart $\mathrm{ι Fin}$, and for every $\hat\jmath \in O$ one has $\mathrm{to}\kappa(\hat\jmath) = a(n)$ in $k$ if and only if the difference of germs at $x_n$ of the $j$-coordinate section over that chart open — obtained from $\mathrm{jChartFin}$ through the chart's $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ and `appIso` identifications and the `app` of the first projection — and of the global constant section coming from $\hat\jmath$ through $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} O)$ and the second projection lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk of $\mathcal X_O$ at $x_n$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the nodes of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over $O$ and the supersingular $j$-invariants in characteristic $p$: the node $n$ sits over the point where $j$ takes the value $a(n)$, expressed as the vanishing of $j - \hat\jmath$ in the local ring at the corresponding point of $\mathcal X_O$. It is used in the determination of the widths and $j$-pinning of the nodes, and in producing lifts $\hat\jmath \in O$ of supersingular $j$-invariants adapted to the resolved model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRResolvedModelPackage_exists_node_equiv_ssJSet_germ_sub_mem_maximalIdeal_iff.lean

